# Step 5 — `refine-logs/EXPERIMENT_PLAN.md` (authoring)

Guidance only; validate still checks non-empty deliverables + manifest (see `research-refine-pipeline.manifest.example.desc`).

Plan is for **idea-creator rank 1** only; align with `FINAL_PROPOSAL.md` and rank-1 title.

## Verification gate (mandatory before “writing dead”)

Every **official URL** listed under data access must be **checked in this run** (fetch or browser): page loads (not 404/5xx), content matches the named dataset. If not checked, label the URL **`TBD — verify:`** + search starting point; **do not** present broken or guessed links as official.

**Data usability:** Only state that data is obtainable (portal, DUA, password channel) if the **same verified page or DOI landing** says so. Do not invent FTP hosts, `*.github.io` mirrors, version folders (e.g. `v1.2/`), archive sizes, or directory trees unless **verified on the official site or after a real download**. Wrong URLs fail delivery quality even when validate passes.

Passwords, tokens, and cohort N from outcome modeling: never fabricate; **TBD** + official contact/DUA text.

## First section (required)

Right after `#` title, the **first H2** must be:

    ## Data access and workspace layout

Include these four H3 subsections (each non-empty):

| H3 | Content |
|----|---------|
| `### Dataset and official sources` | Dataset name; **verified** landing URL(s); download DOI/portal if separate; DUA/license; citation. Example (REST-meta-MDD): landing `https://rfmri.org/REST-meta-MDD`, download `http://doi.org/10.57760/sciencedb.o00115.00013`, DUA contact per that page (e.g. `rfmrilab@gmail.com`) — use only after fetch confirms pages load. |
| `### How to obtain the data` | Ordered steps from **verified** instructions only. If steps were not executed in this run, heading line **`Planned procedure (not yet executed)`** and no fake credentials or timings. |
| `### What you receive after download` | Directory tree, sizes, file types, QC checklist **only after download** or **quoted from official docs** with source link. Otherwise: one line **TBD until first download** + what will be recorded in `data/<slug>/README.md`. |
| `### Where to put files in this project` | Paths **relative to workspace root** (contains `RESEARCH_BRIEF.md`), e.g. `data/rest-meta-mdd/README.md`, `raw/`, phenotypic/derivatives. No machine-specific roots (`/root/...`). No secrets in git. |

Then continue with study question, Phase 0, etc. Phase 0 “obtain data” should **reference this section**, not duplicate URLs.
